    "result_text": "The cable-mean figure now shows in the footer of the people sheet, and `bin/e2e` passes: the test reads `251` from `rollup-cable-mean`.\n\nThe change is only in the front end, in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people-list.ts`:\n- **New row:** a \"Cable mean\" row under \"Cable even\", labelled `rollup-cable-mean`. It shows `n/a` when no one has a cable value.\n- **New calculation:** `cableMean` averages the cable of the people not on hold, skips anyone whose cable is n/a, and rounds with the same `divide` helper as every other average. It's built the same way as the existing means, like knot mean.\n\nThe server and stored data didn't need changes, because each person's cable value was already sent to the page.",
